From dc775ff26866a85fc7cf74e8ba1162facecb6e85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Larry Reynolds <larry.jr.design@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:40:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign Style Stacks panel around a searchable class list;
 add import and export

The panel stacked apply, manage, save, library and feedback into one long
column with three nested scroll areas, so it stopped working past about
five classes. It's now list-first:

- Fixed header (search, selection status) and one scrolling list. Results
  show as a toast at the bottom of the visible panel, not below the fold.
- Classes group by source (this file, then each library) and by slash
  folder, with collapsible groups and search across all of them. Rows show
  small icons for what each class contains; "Published" marks this file's
  library classes.
- Saving moves to its own view behind +, with the portability warning
  inline before saving.
- A details view replaces the inline edit box: preview, contents with
  token names, rename, update from selection, add to library, export,
  delete.
- Header menu: import classes, export all, export selected.
- Import reviews the file first (name clashes: keep both, replace or
  skip) and matches variables and styles to this file by key, so imported
  ids never point at the wrong local variable.
- 11px minimum text, no focusable elements nested in buttons, theme colors
  from Figma's variables for light and dark.

code.ts sends a per-class summary (preview CSS and readable contents) and
handles export, import-preview and import messages.

